{
 "ep": 25,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Tablespaces: When and Why",
 "phase": "Installation & Administration",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Should you move PostgreSQL tables to another disk?",
   "cap": "Should you move tables to *another disk?*"
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode twenty five of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: tablespaces, and their risks.",
   "cap": "Episode 25: *tablespaces,* when and why.",
   "cue": "tablespaces"
  },
  {
   "say": "A tablespace is a named directory where PostgreSQL stores data files for tables, indexes or databases.",
   "cap": "A *tablespace* = a named *directory* for data files.",
   "cue": "directory"
  },
  {
   "say": "Every cluster has two built in: pg_default for normal data, and pg_global for shared catalogs.",
   "cap": "Built in: *pg_default* and *pg_global.*",
   "cue": "pg_default"
  },
  {
   "say": "The docs give two reasons to add one. First, the main volume runs out of space and cannot be extended.",
   "cap": "Reason 1: the volume is *full.*",
   "cue": "space"
  },
  {
   "say": "Second: a busy index on a fast disk, and rarely used archive data on a cheaper one.",
   "cap": "Reason 2: *busy index* fast, *archive* slow.",
   "cue": "busy"
  },
  {
   "say": "Let's build one. The directory must exist, should be empty, and must be owned by the PostgreSQL system user.",
   "cap": "Directory: *exists,* *empty,* owned by *postgres.*",
   "cue": "owned"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then a superuser runs CREATE TABLESPACE fastspace with that location.",
   "cap": "*Superuser:* CREATE TABLESPACE ... LOCATION",
   "cue": "CREATE"
  },
  {
   "say": "PostgreSQL will not create the directory for you. The error says: directory does not exist.",
   "cap": "Missing directory: *does not exist.*",
   "cue": "error"
  },
  {
   "say": "psql's backslash d b command now lists the new tablespace.",
   "cap": "*\\db* lists *fastspace.*",
   "cue": "lists"
  },
  {
   "say": "And in the data directory, pg_tblspc holds a symbolic link to it. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "*pg_tblspc* holds a *symlink.*",
   "cue": "symbolic"
  },
  {
   "say": "Now move a table. ALTER TABLE orders SET TABLESPACE fastspace.",
   "cap": "*ALTER TABLE* ... *SET TABLESPACE*",
   "cue": "ALTER"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_relation_filepath went from base to pg_tblspc. The data file moved.",
   "cap": "File path: *base* to *pg_tblspc.*",
   "cue": "moved"
  },
  {
   "say": "Watch out: indexes are not moved. orders_pkey stayed in base until ALTER INDEX moved it.",
   "cap": "*Indexes are not moved* with the table.",
   "cue": "INDEX"
  },
  {
   "say": "The move holds an access exclusive lock, as pg_locks shows. Even reads wait until it commits.",
   "cap": "Moving takes an *ACCESS EXCLUSIVE* lock.",
   "cue": "pg_locks"
  },
  {
   "say": "Users need the CREATE privilege on it. Without it, app_user got: permission denied for tablespace fastspace.",
   "cap": "No CREATE privilege: *permission denied.*",
   "cue": "permission"
  },
  {
   "say": "After GRANT CREATE ON TABLESPACE, the same CREATE TABLE worked.",
   "cap": "*GRANT CREATE ON TABLESPACE* fixes it.",
   "cue": "worked"
  },
  {
   "say": "default_tablespace places new tables and indexes that have no TABLESPACE clause.",
   "cap": "*default_tablespace:* where new objects go.",
   "cue": "TABLESPACE"
  },
  {
   "say": "temp_tablespaces does the same for temp tables and the temporary files of big sorts.",
   "cap": "*temp_tablespaces:* temp tables and *sort files.*",
   "cue": "sorts"
  },
  {
   "say": "Big warning: a tablespace is part of the cluster. You cannot attach it elsewhere or back it up alone.",
   "cap": "Part of the cluster. *Never standalone.*",
   "cue": "warning"
  },
  {
   "say": "Lose that disk, and the cluster might not start. Never use a ram disk or removable storage.",
   "cap": "Lose it: cluster *may not start.*",
   "cue": "ram"
  },
  {
   "say": "In plain format, pg_basebackup writes each tablespace to the same path, unless you use tablespace mapping.",
   "cap": "*pg_basebackup:* same paths, or *tablespace mapping.*",
   "cue": "mapping"
  },
  {
   "say": "Myth: tablespaces are automatic tuning. They are only locations, and two on one file system usually gain little.",
   "cap": "Myth: tablespace = *speed.* It is a *location.*",
   "cue": "location"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: a location, not a tuning knob. Reliable storage, grant CREATE, move indexes too, and plan for the lock.",
   "cap": "Recap: *location,* not a *tuning knob.*",
   "cue": "grant"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: PostgreSQL extensions, how to install and manage them. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *extensions.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
